{"id": "EUVD-2026-86123", "enisaUuid": "f7e6d182-81cb-32a5-9573-d994af1415eb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nACPI: bus: Introduce acpi_bus_get_primary_device()\n\nThe function used for obtaining the first \"physical\" device for which\nthe given ACPI one is the ACPI companion, acpi_get_first_physical_node(),\nmay return a stale device pointer (mostly in theory) because\nacpi_unbind_one() may run as a whole after dropping the ACPI device's\nphysical_node_lock in acpi_get_first_physical_node() and before it\nreturns.  The last reference to the \"physical\" device may be dropped\nthen before the pointer to it is returned to the caller.\n\nIf that happens and the acpi_get_first_physical_node() caller invokes\nget_device() on the pointer obtained from it, which is done by the\nmajority of its callers, a use-after-free will occur.\n\nTo prepare for addressing this problem, introduce a new function for\ngetting the first \"physical\" device associated with the given ACPI one\n(the \"primary physical device\") that will also reference count the\ndevice in question before returning a pointer to it.\n\nMake that new function and acpi_get_first_physical_node() share the\nphysical node list lookup code.\n\nNo intentional functional impact.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:51:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50ddd82b88b1d1cc467b5df953344c1a9feec268", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd4f907b558721716da30acd6630191acf811b95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ebdd932dc24c1cf7cc31710b7730515e4e66d886", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5657859851abb65105220a6cdb5804926249f714", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72530e1f72b0515a73fd88292254d04fecf03649"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2qvg-p8g6-fm8w", "CVE-2026-93251"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cb5ca25-266a-36cb-98ad-abb0076ed2fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91e5687805885f9fceb60b95e950a3d3bdcf4764 <50ddd82b88b1d1cc467b5df953344c1a9feec268"}, {"id": "0d55d510-7b2c-3c76-8271-db84a9344ccf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91e5687805885f9fceb60b95e950a3d3bdcf4764 <ebdd932dc24c1cf7cc31710b7730515e4e66d886"}, {"id": "2513afc6-1626-310e-81d2-a0d80d126d09", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "2fe45f2f-11fc-3eda-b189-bb1a8ff7e47e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91e5687805885f9fceb60b95e950a3d3bdcf4764 <fd4f907b558721716da30acd6630191acf811b95"}, {"id": "327ab5be-2777-3553-ac91-2af1c8cd4997", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4bab794a-72e3-34f6-9f82-49dfcdadd052", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "4d10cf03-5175-33a8-b005-c037052deba1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "60974c17-1f82-35f8-befe-3fdcc8c3cf7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91e5687805885f9fceb60b95e950a3d3bdcf4764 <72530e1f72b0515a73fd88292254d04fecf03649"}, {"id": "a13b4be2-89b1-3f0d-8039-5c4b7ee2feaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "91e5687805885f9fceb60b95e950a3d3bdcf4764 <5657859851abb65105220a6cdb5804926249f714"}, {"id": "a6e74674-b40e-3406-b9e9-c174df08fca3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "f1d3cb6b-99a6-31f8-999a-773c209d1d47", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "fb52eb9d-2830-3f88-8e1e-af4b91eded6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dba7f224-865b-3d4d-bc